**What AGPL-3.0 means in practice for this project.** The AGPL's defining
feature — relative to the ordinary GPL — is section 13: if you run a *modified*
version of this program on a server and let users interact with it **over a
network**, you must offer those users the corresponding source code. Running
the program locally, or distributing unmodified binaries, triggers the usual
GPL obligations instead.

